---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { APP_STORE_URL, DEMO_URL } from '../consts';

const title = 'Merchandising solutions — QSortby for Shopify';
const description =
  'Every catalog moves on a different signal. QSortby merchandises each one by the one that matters — trend, intent, conversion or live inventory.';
const check = '<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="phero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="crumb"><a href="/">~</a> / solutions</div>
      <h1>Merchandised by what actually moves <em>your</em> catalog.</h1>
      <p>Fast launches live on momentum. Discovery catalogs live on intent. Lookalike ranges live on proof. Limited stock lives on availability. Big catalogs live on scale. QSortby sorts each one by the signal that moves it — automatically.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec">
    <div class="wrap ucs">

      <!-- ===== FAST LAUNCHES — trending velocity + sold-out variants ===== -->
      <article class="uc rv">
        <div class="uc-copy">
          <span class="tag">Fast-moving launches</span>
          <h3>Lead with what's trending this week — not last season.</h3>
          <p>Drops and new arrivals live and die on momentum. QSortby ranks by <b>trending velocity</b>, so the product catching fire rises to the front the moment it moves — and the variant that just sold out steps aside before it kills a click.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Trending velocity over a window you set</li>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Sold-out variants demoted instantly</li>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> A fresh front row every launch</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="uc-panel">
          <span class="uc-cap" data-c="trend">Trending this launch</span>
          <div class="uc-stage uc-trend">
            <div class="gcard tr-row tr-a"><span class="gthumb"><img src="/products/sneaker.svg" alt="" /></span><span class="tr-nm">Trail Runner</span><span class="tr-tag sold">Sold out · size M</span></div>
            <div class="gcard tr-row tr-b"><span class="gthumb"><img src="/products/cap.svg" alt="" /></span><span class="tr-nm">Canvas Cap</span><span class="tr-tag up">▲ Trending</span></div>
            <div class="gcard tr-row tr-c"><span class="gthumb"><img src="/products/headphones.svg" alt="" /></span><span class="tr-nm">Studio Headphones</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- ===== DISCOVERY CATALOGS — Emotional AI / intent ===== -->
      <article class="uc rev rv">
        <div class="uc-copy">
          <span class="tag">Discovery-driven catalogs</span>
          <h3>Turn browsing into discovery.</h3>
          <p>In some categories shoppers buy on feel and can't name what they want. QSortby reads <b>on-site intent</b> — what they linger on, revisit, compare — and surfaces the product they're most likely to fall for.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Reads passive intent signals</li>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Surfaces a different order per shopper</li>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Per-category bestsellers stay fresh</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="uc-panel">
          <span class="uc-cap" data-c="intent">Reading intent</span>
          <div class="uc-stage uc-int">
            <div class="bi-sigs"><span class="bi-sig s1">gifting</span><span class="bi-sig s2">comparing</span><span class="bi-sig s3">returning</span></div>
            <div class="bi-meter"><i></i></div>
            <span class="bi-lbl">Match found</span>
            <div class="gcard bi-rec"><span class="gthumb"><img src="/products/headphones.svg" alt="" /></span><span class="tr-nm">Studio Headphones</span><span class="bi-tag">Surface</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- ===== LOOKALIKE RANGES — velocity / conversion ===== -->
      <article class="uc rv">
        <div class="uc-copy">
          <span class="tag">Wide, lookalike ranges</span>
          <h3>Lead with proven sellers, not a flat grid.</h3>
          <p>When forty products look near-identical on a grid, position decides the sale. QSortby sorts by <b>sales velocity and conversion rate</b> — so the variants that actually close move to the front, and the lookalikes that don't quietly sink.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Sort by sales velocity or conversion</li>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Proven sellers &amp; bundles up front</li>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Insights on what truly converts</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="uc-panel">
          <span class="uc-cap" data-c="rev">Sort · Bestselling</span>
          <div class="uc-stage uc-rev">
            <div class="rv-row rv-a gcard"><span class="gthumb"><img src="/products/mug.svg" alt="" /></span><span class="tr-nm">Ceramic Mug</span><span class="rv-bar"><i style="--w:38%"></i></span><span class="rv-amt">$2.1k</span></div>
            <div class="rv-row rv-b gcard win"><span class="gthumb"><img src="/products/tee.svg" alt="" /></span><span class="tr-nm">Everyday Tee</span><span class="rv-bar"><i style="--w:100%"></i></span><span class="rv-amt">$8.4k</span><span class="rv-cvr">3.2× CVR</span></div>
            <div class="rv-row rv-c gcard"><span class="gthumb"><img src="/products/tote.svg" alt="" /></span><span class="tr-nm">Canvas Tote</span><span class="rv-bar"><i style="--w:62%"></i></span><span class="rv-amt">$4.7k</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- ===== LIMITED / SEASONAL STOCK — inventory-aware ===== -->
      <article class="uc rev rv">
        <div class="uc-copy">
          <span class="tag">Limited &amp; seasonal stock</span>
          <h3>Only feature what's actually buyable.</h3>
          <p>Seasonal ranges and small-batch runs mean availability matters as much as popularity. QSortby pairs sales velocity with <b>live inventory</b>: when stock runs low it demotes before it sells out, and promotes the moment you restock.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Inventory-aware ranking</li>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Low stock demotes before it's gone</li>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Restock auto-promotes back up</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="uc-panel">
          <span class="uc-cap" data-c="stock">Live inventory</span>
          <div class="uc-stage uc-stock">
            <div class="st-row st-a gcard"><span class="gthumb"><img src="/products/bottle.svg" alt="" /></span><span class="tr-nm">Steel Water Bottle</span><span class="st-bar"><i class="ok"></i></span><span class="st-pill ok">In stock</span></div>
            <div class="st-row st-b gcard"><span class="gthumb"><img src="/products/jar.svg" alt="" /></span><span class="tr-nm">Daily Moisturizer</span><span class="st-bar"><i class="low"></i></span><span class="st-pill no">Low → out</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- ===== LARGE CATALOGS — auto-curation at scale ===== -->
      <article class="uc rv">
        <div class="uc-copy">
          <span class="tag">Large catalogs &amp; bundles</span>
          <h3>Make a huge catalog feel hand-picked.</h3>
          <p>Thousands of SKUs are impossible to merchandise by hand. QSortby <b>auto-curates at scale</b> — every collection arranges itself by what's actually selling, so hundreds of products look like someone hand-picked the front row.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Hands-off curation at scale</li>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Per-collection rules</li>
            <li><span set:html={check} /> Always-fresh homepage rows</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="uc-panel">
          <span class="uc-cap" data-c="curate">Auto-curated</span>
          <div class="uc-stage uc-curate">
            <span class="cu-tile c1"><img src="/products/box.svg" alt="" /></span>
            <span class="cu-tile c2"><img src="/products/mug.svg" alt="" /></span>
            <span class="cu-tile c3"><img src="/products/watch.svg" alt="" /></span>
            <span class="cu-tile c4"><img src="/products/bottle.svg" alt="" /></span>
            <span class="cu-tile c5"><img src="/products/tote.svg" alt="" /></span>
            <span class="cu-tile c6"><img src="/products/tee.svg" alt="" /></span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta rv">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Get started</span>
        <h2>Sorted for <em>your</em> catalog.</h2>
        <p>Install free and point QSortby at one collection — by the signal that matters most to you.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta" style="justify-content:center">
          <a href={APP_STORE_URL} class="btn btn-accent btn-lg">Install free <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>
          <a href={DEMO_URL} class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg">Book a demo</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
